AGENTS.md:3:tentacles runs coding-agent sessions remotely, on pi-durable, over infrastructure behind provider-neutral contracts, with Cloudflare as the first setup. A plugin for pi and Claude Code lets a local agent spawn, steer, question and collect those remote sessions the way it does local subagents.
docs/invariants.md:16:- A session's status changes only in reaction to its pi-durable session, except a failed workspace setup at spawn, which marks the session failed before its first run ([sessions](technical-design/sessions.md)).
docs/invariants.md:24:- A session's alarm belongs to pi-durable, to resume a run after an eviction; nothing else schedules on it ([sessions](technical-design/sessions.md)).
docs/technical-design/providers/cloudflare/computer-workspace.md:35:The workspace's files live in the session Durable Object's SQLite, next to pi-durable's tables. computerd mounts them in the container at `/workspace` through FUSE, so `/workspace/repo`, `/workspace/skills` and `/workspace/context` have the same paths for the file tools, the shell and the container. Only `/workspace` is shared: anything the container writes elsewhere sits on the container's own disk and is lost when the container stops. The runtimes mise installs live outside `/workspace`, so the agent installs them again after a stop.
docs/technical-design/providers/cloudflare/deploy.md:11:On Cloudflare, tentacles runs as one Worker that is the only entry point, one registry Durable Object for everything that spans sessions, one session Durable Object per session running pi-durable and holding the session's Computer workspace, a Codemode Worker for codemode scripts, and one Claude container shared by every session. Models other than Claude go through AI Gateway, and the preview's browser is a Browser Run browser opened through a binding. No container holds a credential: the workspace's git client and egress gateway add the GitHub token, and the Claude container's outbound handler adds the subscription token. One Alchemy stack declares every resource.
docs/technical-design/providers/cloudflare/deploy.md:23:        Session@{ shape: rect, label: "Session DO<br/>pi-durable Harness, SQLite,<br/>socket, alarm,<br/>Computer workspace, git client,<br/>egress gateway with the CDP relay" }
docs/technical-design/providers/cloudflare/deploy.md:73:Each session is one Durable Object keyed by its session id, and it fills five roles: `SessionHost`, `SessionStorage` (its SQLite), `WakeTimer` (its alarm), `ParentChannel` (its WebSockets) and `Workspace`. It runs pi-durable's Harness over its SQLite, with the question tool and the `onWake` alarm that resumes a run after an eviction. At spawn it builds the session's Computer workspace in the same SQLite storage and runs its setup; from then on the workspace's files, its git client and its container live in the object ([computer-workspace](computer-workspace.md)). The egress gateway that handles the container's outbound requests, including the CDP relay, also runs in the object. It sends each model call where the session's settings say: Claude models to the shared Claude container, other providers to AI Gateway through `env.AI`. It opens and closes the preview's Browser Run browser through its own binding. The daily cleanup job deletes a session through its Durable Object, which clears the object's storage, the workspace's files included, then removes the session's registry entry itself.
docs/technical-design/providers/cloudflare/deploy.md:84:The scripts the agent writes with its codemode tool run in pi-durable's QuickJS sandbox, in a sandbox Durable Object of a separate Worker, which the Worker binds by name. Each session's scripts reach it from the session object, through the `CodeSandbox` contract, and call the workspace's tools by name.
docs/technical-design/question-round-trip.md:50:A prompt sent while a question waits is a steer whatever mode the parent sends it with, and reaches the agent after the answer; a prompt neither answers nor cancels the question. A question keeps its id when an eviction makes the tool run again, so an answer sent for it still resolves it. Every eviction cuts the waiting tool call off, and pi-durable counts each cut-off toward its restart limit. The session lifts that limit while the question's call is live, so the question survives any number of evictions. An answer to a question that is not waiting returns an error, which the parent sees as a tool failure.
docs/technical-design/runtime-components.md:11:tentacles runs as a set of roles: an API entry that is the only way in, a registry for everything that spans sessions, one session object per session running pi-durable, a workspace per session that holds the agent's files and runs its commands, model providers, a codemode sandbox, a managed browser for previews and a daily scheduler. tentacles' shared logic reaches each role through a contract, and a provider fills every contract, so another setup can replace the infrastructure without changing the plugin. No container holds a credential: the provider adds the tokens to requests outside the container. Cloudflare is the first provider; [deploy](providers/cloudflare/deploy.md) covers how it fills each role.
docs/technical-design/runtime-components.md:23:        Session@{ shape: rect, label: "Session object<br/>pi-durable Harness, storage,<br/>socket, wake-up timer" }
docs/technical-design/runtime-components.md:58:The **session object** is one live instance per session, keyed by its session id. It runs pi-durable's Harness over its own storage, with the question tool and the wake-up timer that resumes a run after an eviction. It creates the session's workspace at spawn and installs the tools the workspace returns, holds the parent's socket, sends each model call to the provider the settings name, and opens and closes the preview's browser. It never writes the status ahead of the run: it watches pi-durable's state and tells the registry each time the derived status changes.
docs/technical-design/runtime-components.md:66:Each component above plays a role that any provider has to fill. Several roles already sit behind an interface the pi libraries define: pi-durable takes its storage, its wake-up timer and its tools from the host, and pi-ai reaches models through providers. The plugin talks only to the Worker API and the session socket, so it does not change with the provider.
